3D Visualization: 3D Slicer basic exmpale code
3D Slicer is the standard open-source workstation for medical image visualization. While you can use the GUI, the Slicer Python API allows you to automate data loading and 3D rendering.
To run this, open 3D Slicer, go to the Python Interactor (Ctrl+3), and paste the code.
🛠️ Basic 3D Loading & Volume Rendering
python
import SampleData

# 1. Load a sample 3D dataset (CT Chest)
# This returns the 'MRML' node which represents the data in Slicer
volumeNode = SampleData.downloadSample('CTChest')

# 2. Setup 3D Volume Rendering
volRenLogic = slicer.modules.volumerendering.logic()
displayNode = volRenLogic.CreateDefaultVolumeRenderingNodes(volumeNode)

# 3. Apply a "Preset" to make it look like a real 3D medical scan
# Common presets: 'CT-Muscle', 'CT-Bone', 'CT-Air'
shaderProperty = displayNode.GetVolumePropertyNode().GetShaderProperty()
displayNode.GetVolumePropertyNode().Copy(volRenLogic.GetPresetByName('CT-Bone'))

# 4. Center the 3D view
layoutManager = slicer.app.layoutManager()
threeDWidget = layoutManager.threeDWidget(0)
threeDView = threeDWidget.threeDView()
threeDView.resetFocalPoint()

print(f"Successfully rendered 3D Volume: {volumeNode.GetName()}")
Use code with caution.

🔑 Essential Slicer Scripting Concepts
MRML Nodes: Everything in Slicer is a MRML (Medical Reality Markup Language) node. Images are vtkMRMLScalarVolumeNode, and segmentations are vtkMRMLSegmentationNode.
The Logic Layer: Modules in Slicer have a "Logic" class (e.g., slicer.modules.volumes.logic()) that handles background operations like file I/O or processing.
MONAI Integration: You can connect Slicer to your AI models using the MONAI Label extension. This allows you to run your trained PyTorch models directly on the 3D volume in Slicer.
🚀 Advanced: Scripting Segmentations
If you want to visualize specific organs (like your MONAI spleen segmentation), you use the Segmentation Node:
python
# Create a new segmentation node
segNode = slicer.mrmlScene.AddNewNodeByClass("vtkMRMLSegmentationNode")
segNode.CreateDefaultDisplayNodes()
segNode.SetReferenceImageGeometryParameterFromVolumeNode(volumeNode)
